I"��<h2 class="no_toc" id="65-introducción-a-la-arquitectura-de-microservicios">6.5. Introducción a la arquitectura de microservicios</h2>

<ul id="markdown-toc">
  <li><a href="#651-creación-de-dos-microservicios-independientes" id="markdown-toc-651-creación-de-dos-microservicios-independientes">6.5.1. Creación de dos microservicios independientes</a></li>
  <li><a href="#653-comunicación-http-entre-microservicios-con-httpx" id="markdown-toc-653-comunicación-http-entre-microservicios-con-httpx">6.5.3. Comunicación HTTP entre microservicios con httpx</a></li>
  <li><a href="#654-middlewares" id="markdown-toc-654-middlewares">6.5.4. Middlewares</a></li>
</ul>

<p><a href="https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/xemg6hf7l8armzlnobb0v/06_05_arquitectura_microservicios.pdf?rlkey=cs2abynmsm5cqrx9xav30th06&amp;st=89xo1udg&amp;dl=0" class="btn btn-primary">Descargar presentación</a></p>

<p>A lo largo de este curso has hecho muchas cosas y montado muchas aplicaciones de servidor. Unas estaban diseñadas para ser usadas directamente por personas (aplicaciones tipo SSR, que generan vistas) y otras para ser consumidas por un frontend.</p>

<p>Lo que todavía no has hecho es crear un backend diseñado para <em>ser consumido por otro backend</em>. Es decir, crear <strong>dos servicios diferentes que colaboren entre sí</strong>.</p>

<p>Eso es justo lo que vamos a hacer ahora con FastAPI, y, con ello, uniremos todo lo que hemos visto sobre microservicios:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Lenguaje Python</li>
  <li>Endpoints con validación automática</li>
  <li>Persistencia de datos con SQLAlchemy</li>
  <li>Inyección de dependencias</li>
  <li>Asincronía.</li>
</ul>

<p>Vamos a trabajar sobre un ejemplo: construiremos <strong>dos microservicios independientes</strong>, de manera que uno consultará al otro por HTTP.</p>

<p>Como son microservicios, deben ser pequeños y simples: uno se encargará de gestionar <strong>usuarios</strong> y otro de gestionar <strong>pedidos</strong>.</p>

<h3 id="651-creación-de-dos-microservicios-independientes">6.5.1. Creación de dos microservicios independientes</h3>

<h4 id="estructura-general">Estructura general</h4>

<p>Cada microservicio será un proyecto autónomo, con su propio entorno virtual, sus propias dependencias (<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">requirements.txt</code>) y su propia base de datos:</p>

<div class="language-text highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>tienda/
├── usuarios/                  # Servicio A (puerto 8001)
│   ├── main.py
│   ├── database.py
│   ├── models.py
│   ├── schemas.py
│   ├── requirements.txt
│   └── .venv/
└── pedidos/                   # Servicio B (puerto 8002)
    ├── main.py
    ├── database.py
    ├── models.py
    ├── schemas.py
    ├── requirements.txt
    └── .venv/
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Ambos usan la misma organización que ya conocemos (modelo, esquema, ruta y <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Depends</code>).</p>

<p>El <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">database.py</code> de cada uno es idéntico, cambiando solo el nombre por defecto del archivo SQLite: (<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">sqlite:///./usuarios.db</code> en uno y <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">sqlite:///./pedidos.db</code> en el otro). Así tienes dos bases de datos separadas, como exige la arquitectura.</p>

<p>Para <strong>crear cada proyecto</strong>:</p>

<div class="language-bash highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="nb">cd </span>usuarios
python <span class="nt">-m</span> venv .venv
<span class="nb">source</span> .venv/bin/activate              <span class="c"># (o la variante de Windows)</span>
pip <span class="nb">install </span>fastapi <span class="s2">"uvicorn[standard]"</span> sqlalchemy
pip freeze <span class="o">&gt;</span> requirements.txt
</code></pre></div></div>

<h4 id="servicio-a-usuarios">Servicio A: usuarios</h4>

<p>Se encargará de <strong>registrar y consultar usuarios</strong>.</p>

<p><em>(En una aplicación completa sería también el lugar natural para el login y la emisión de tokens, pero lo dejamos fuera para centrarnos en la comunicación entre servicios).</em></p>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">models.py</code>:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">sqlalchemy</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">String</span>
<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">sqlalchemy.orm</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span>

<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">database</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Base</span>


<span class="k">class</span> <span class="nc">Usuario</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">Base</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">__tablename__</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="s">"usuarios"</span>

    <span class="nb">id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">int</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">primary_key</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">nombre</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">50</span><span class="p">))</span>
    <span class="n">email</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">100</span><span class="p">),</span> <span class="n">unique</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">activo</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">bool</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">default</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">schemas.py</code>:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">pydantic</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">BaseModel</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">ConfigDict</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">Field</span>


<span class="k">class</span> <span class="nc">UsuarioCrear</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">BaseModel</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">nombre</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">str</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">Field</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">min_length</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">max_length</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">50</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">email</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">str</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">Field</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">min_length</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">5</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">max_length</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">100</span><span class="p">)</span>


<span class="k">class</span> <span class="nc">UsuarioRespuesta</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">UsuarioCrear</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">model_config</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">ConfigDict</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">from_attributes</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>

    <span class="nb">id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">int</span>
    <span class="n">activo</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">bool</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">main.py</code>:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">typing</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Annotated</span>

<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">fastapi</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Depends</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">FastAPI</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span>
<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">sqlalchemy</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">select</span>
<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">sqlalchemy.orm</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Session</span>

<span class="kn">import</span> <span class="nn">models</span>
<span class="kn">import</span> <span class="nn">schemas</span>
<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">database</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Base</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">engine</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">get_db</span>

<span class="n">Base</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">metadata</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">create_all</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">bind</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">engine</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">app</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">FastAPI</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">title</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"Servicio de usuarios"</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">SesionDB</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">Annotated</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">Session</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">Depends</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">get_db</span><span class="p">)]</span>


<span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">post</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/usuarios"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">201</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">response_model</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">UsuarioRespuesta</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">crear_usuario</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">datos</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">UsuarioCrear</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">SesionDB</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">existente</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">scalar</span><span class="p">(</span>
        <span class="n">select</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Usuario</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="n">where</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Usuario</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">email</span> <span class="o">==</span> <span class="n">datos</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">email</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">if</span> <span class="n">existente</span><span class="p">:</span>
        <span class="k">raise</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">409</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">detail</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"Ya existe un usuario con ese email"</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">nuevo</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Usuario</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="o">**</span><span class="n">datos</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">model_dump</span><span class="p">())</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">add</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">nuevo</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">commit</span><span class="p">()</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">refresh</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">nuevo</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">nuevo</span>


<span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/usuarios"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">response_model</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="nb">list</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">UsuarioRespuesta</span><span class="p">])</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">listar_usuarios</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">db</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">SesionDB</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">scalars</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">select</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Usuario</span><span class="p">)).</span><span class="nb">all</span><span class="p">()</span>


<span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/usuarios/{usuario_id}"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">response_model</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">UsuarioRespuesta</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">obtener_usuario</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">int</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">SesionDB</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">usuario</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Usuario</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">if</span> <span class="n">usuario</span> <span class="ow">is</span> <span class="bp">None</span><span class="p">:</span>
        <span class="k">raise</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">404</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">detail</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"Usuario no encontrado"</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">usuario</span>


<span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">patch</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/usuarios/{usuario_id}/desactivar"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">response_model</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">UsuarioRespuesta</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">desactivar_usuario</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">int</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">SesionDB</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">usuario</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Usuario</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">if</span> <span class="n">usuario</span> <span class="ow">is</span> <span class="bp">None</span><span class="p">:</span>
        <span class="k">raise</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">404</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">detail</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"Usuario no encontrado"</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">usuario</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">activo</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="bp">False</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">commit</span><span class="p">()</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">refresh</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">usuario</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p><strong>Al arrancarlo</strong>, no olvides colocarlo en su puerto:</p>

<div class="language-bash highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>uvicorn main:app <span class="nt">--port</span> 8001 <span class="nt">--reload</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Comprueba en <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">http://127.0.0.1:8001/docs</code> que funciona y crea un par de usuarios.</p>

<h4 id="servicio-b-pedidos">Servicio B: pedidos</h4>

<p>Este microservicio gestionará los <strong>pedidos de los usuarios</strong>.</p>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">models.py</code>:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">sqlalchemy</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">String</span>
<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">sqlalchemy.orm</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span>

<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">database</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Base</span>


<span class="k">class</span> <span class="nc">Pedido</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">Base</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">__tablename__</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="s">"pedidos"</span>

    <span class="nb">id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">int</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">primary_key</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">int</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">index</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>    <span class="c1"># ¡sin ForeignKey!
</span>    <span class="n">descripcion</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">200</span><span class="p">))</span>
    <span class="n">importe</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">float</span><span class="p">]</span>
    <span class="n">estado</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Mapped</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">mapped_column</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">20</span><span class="p">),</span> <span class="n">default</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"pendiente"</span><span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Observa un momento <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">usuario_id</code>. En un monolito con Laravel o Spring Boot, lo habitual sería declararlo como <strong>clave foránea</strong> apuntando a la tabla de usuarios, y la base de datos garantizaría que no existen pedidos de usuarios inexistentes. ¡Pero aquí <strong>no podemos hacer eso</strong> porque <strong>la tabla de usuarios está en otra base de datos</strong>!</p>

<p>Por eso <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">usuario_id</code> es simplemente un número y la integridad referencia debe gestionarla y garantizarla tu aplicación.</p>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">schemas.py</code>:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">pydantic</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">BaseModel</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">ConfigDict</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">Field</span>


<span class="k">class</span> <span class="nc">PedidoCrear</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">BaseModel</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">descripcion</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">str</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">Field</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">min_length</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">3</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">max_length</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">200</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">importe</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">float</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">Field</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">gt</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">)</span>


<span class="k">class</span> <span class="nc">PedidoRespuesta</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">PedidoCrear</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">model_config</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">ConfigDict</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">from_attributes</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>

    <span class="nb">id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">int</span>
    <span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">int</span>
    <span class="n">estado</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">str</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">main.py</code> (primera versión, <em>todavía sin comunicarse con el otro servicio</em>).</p>

<p>Vamos a modelar los pedidos como un <strong>“subrecurso”</strong> de los usuarios (<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">/usuarios/{id}/pedidos</code>), aunque podríamos crear las rutas de cualquier otra manera:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">typing</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Annotated</span>

<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">fastapi</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Depends</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">FastAPI</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span>
<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">sqlalchemy</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">select</span>
<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">sqlalchemy.orm</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Session</span>

<span class="kn">import</span> <span class="nn">models</span>
<span class="kn">import</span> <span class="nn">schemas</span>
<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">database</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Base</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">engine</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">get_db</span>

<span class="n">Base</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">metadata</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">create_all</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">bind</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">engine</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">app</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">FastAPI</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">title</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"Servicio de pedidos"</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">SesionDB</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">Annotated</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">Session</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">Depends</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">get_db</span><span class="p">)]</span>


<span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">post</span><span class="p">(</span>
    <span class="s">"/usuarios/{usuario_id}/pedidos"</span><span class="p">,</span>
    <span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">201</span><span class="p">,</span>
    <span class="n">response_model</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">PedidoRespuesta</span><span class="p">,</span>
<span class="p">)</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">crear_pedido</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">int</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">datos</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">PedidoCrear</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">SesionDB</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">nuevo</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Pedido</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="o">**</span><span class="n">datos</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">model_dump</span><span class="p">())</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">add</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">nuevo</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">commit</span><span class="p">()</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">refresh</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">nuevo</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">nuevo</span>


<span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span>
    <span class="s">"/usuarios/{usuario_id}/pedidos"</span><span class="p">,</span>
    <span class="n">response_model</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="nb">list</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">PedidoRespuesta</span><span class="p">],</span>
<span class="p">)</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">listar_pedidos_de_usuario</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">int</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">SesionDB</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">consulta</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">select</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Pedido</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="n">where</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Pedido</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span> <span class="o">==</span> <span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">scalars</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">consulta</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="nb">all</span><span class="p">()</span>


<span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/pedidos/{pedido_id}"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">response_model</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">PedidoRespuesta</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">obtener_pedido</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">pedido_id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">int</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">SesionDB</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">pedido</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Pedido</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">pedido_id</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">if</span> <span class="n">pedido</span> <span class="ow">is</span> <span class="bp">None</span><span class="p">:</span>
        <span class="k">raise</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">404</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">detail</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"Pedido no encontrado"</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">pedido</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p><strong>Arráncalo</strong> en otro puerto y en otra terminal, con su propio entorno virtual:</p>

<div class="language-bash highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>uvicorn main:app <span class="nt">--port</span> 8002 <span class="nt">--reload</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Ya tenemos dos microservicios corriendo a la vez, cada uno con su documentación (<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">:8001/docs</code> y <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">:8002/docs</code>), su base de datos y su ciclo de vida independiente. Puedes apagar uno sin que el otro se entere.</p>

<p><strong>Pero la versión actual tiene un fallo evidente</strong>: <em>puedes crear un pedido para el usuario <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">999</code>, que no existe</em>. Eso es porque los microservicios no se están comunicando entre sí.</p>

<p>¡Vamos a arreglarlo!</p>

<h3 id="653-comunicación-http-entre-microservicios-con-httpx">6.5.3. Comunicación HTTP entre microservicios con httpx</h3>

<h4 id="qué-es-httpx">Qué es httpx</h4>

<p><strong>httpx</strong> es un cliente HTTP para Python: sirve para que tu código haga peticiones a otros servicios.</p>

<p>Ofrece una API muy sencilla y <strong>funciona tanto en modo síncrono como asíncrono</strong>.</p>

<p>Ten en cuenta que Laravel y Spring Boot también tienen clientes como httpx, solo que en esos frameworks se usan menos, porque los empleamos más para construir grandes monolitos y no pequeños microservicios que, por su naturaleza, necesitan a menuda “hablar” con otros microservicios.</p>

<p><strong>Instala httpx</strong> en el entorno del servicio de <strong>pedidos</strong>:</p>

<div class="language-bash highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>pip <span class="nb">install </span>httpx
pip freeze <span class="o">&gt;</span> requirements.txt
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Aquí puedes ver cómo se usa httpx:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="nn">httpx</span>

<span class="c1"># Modo síncrono (recuerda: usar solo en funciones "def")
</span><span class="n">respuesta</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">httpx</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"http://localhost:8001/usuarios/1"</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="c1"># Modo asíncrono (recuerda: usar solo en funciones "async def")
</span><span class="k">async</span> <span class="k">with</span> <span class="n">httpx</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">AsyncClient</span><span class="p">()</span> <span class="k">as</span> <span class="n">cliente</span><span class="p">:</span>
    <span class="n">respuesta</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="k">await</span> <span class="n">cliente</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"http://localhost:8001/usuarios/1"</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">respuesta</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">status_code</span>     <span class="c1"># 200
</span><span class="n">respuesta</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">json</span><span class="p">()</span>          <span class="c1"># el cuerpo convertido a dict
</span><span class="n">respuesta</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">raise_for_status</span><span class="p">()</span>   <span class="c1"># lanza una excepción si el código es 4xx o 5xx
</span></code></pre></div></div>

<p>httpx ofrece, por supuesto, más funciones. Una muy importante es <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">cliente.post(url, json={...})</code>, para enviar por POST un cuerpo JSON. Dentro de las llaves puedes colocar:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">params={"clave": "valor"}</code> -&gt; para construir la cadena de consulta (query string)</li>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">headers={...}</code> -&gt; para construir cabeceras de la http request.</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="llamada-asíncrona-de-pedidos-a-usuarios">Llamada asíncrona de pedidos a usuarios</h4>

<p>Vamos a crear una llamada HTTP <strong>asíncrona</strong> (<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">await</code>) de pedidos a usuarios, para asegurarnos que el <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">usuario_id</code> del pedido se corresponde con un usuario existente.</p>

<p>Por tanto, necesitará una función <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">async def</code>. Pero el acceso a base de datos del servicio es <strong>síncrono</strong> y, según vimos, no debemos meter operaciones bloqueantes dentro de una <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">async def</code>.</p>

<p>Lo que haremos para solucionar esta aparente contradicción es <strong>hacer asíncrona la comprobación del usuario</strong> pero conservar el endpoint con un <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">def</code> síncrono normal. FastAPI ejecutará cada pieza en el sitio adecuado: la dependencia en el bucle de eventos y el endpoint en un hilo aparte.</p>

<p>Solo tienes que añadir esto al <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">main.py</code> del microservicio de pedidos:</p>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">pedidos/main.py</code></p>
<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="nn">os</span>

<span class="kn">import</span> <span class="nn">httpx</span>

<span class="n">USUARIOS_URL</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">os</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">getenv</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"USUARIOS_URL"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s">"http://localhost:8001"</span><span class="p">)</span>


<span class="k">async</span> <span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">usuario_valido</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="nb">int</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="o">-&gt;</span> <span class="nb">dict</span><span class="p">:</span>
    <span class="s">"""Consulta al servicio de usuarios y comprueba que existe y está activo."""</span>
    <span class="k">try</span><span class="p">:</span>
        <span class="k">async</span> <span class="k">with</span> <span class="n">httpx</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">AsyncClient</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">base_url</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">USUARIOS_URL</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">timeout</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mf">3.0</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="k">as</span> <span class="n">cliente</span><span class="p">:</span>
            <span class="n">respuesta</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="k">await</span> <span class="n">cliente</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sa">f</span><span class="s">"/usuarios/</span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s">"</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">except</span> <span class="n">httpx</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">TimeoutException</span><span class="p">:</span>
        <span class="k">raise</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">504</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">detail</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"El servicio de usuarios tardó demasiado en responder"</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">except</span> <span class="n">httpx</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">RequestError</span><span class="p">:</span>
        <span class="k">raise</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">503</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">detail</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"El servicio de usuarios no está disponible"</span><span class="p">)</span>

    <span class="k">if</span> <span class="n">respuesta</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">status_code</span> <span class="o">==</span> <span class="mi">404</span><span class="p">:</span>
        <span class="k">raise</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">404</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">detail</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"Usuario no encontrado"</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">if</span> <span class="n">respuesta</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">status_code</span> <span class="o">!=</span> <span class="mi">200</span><span class="p">:</span>
        <span class="k">raise</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">502</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">detail</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"Respuesta inesperada del servicio de usuarios"</span><span class="p">)</span>

    <span class="n">usuario</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">respuesta</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">json</span><span class="p">()</span>
    <span class="k">if</span> <span class="ow">not</span> <span class="n">usuario</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="s">"activo"</span><span class="p">]:</span>
        <span class="k">raise</span> <span class="n">HTTPException</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">403</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">detail</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s">"El usuario está desactivado"</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">usuario</span>


<span class="n">UsuarioValido</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">Annotated</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="nb">dict</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">Depends</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario_valido</span><span class="p">)]</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Ahora, <strong>los endpoints que necesitan un usuario válido lo piden con <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UsuarioValido</code></strong> en lugar de recibir directamente <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">usuario_id</code>:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">post</span><span class="p">(</span>
    <span class="s">"/usuarios/{usuario_id}/pedidos"</span><span class="p">,</span>
    <span class="n">status_code</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">201</span><span class="p">,</span>
    <span class="n">response_model</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">PedidoRespuesta</span><span class="p">,</span>
<span class="p">)</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">crear_pedido</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">datos</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">PedidoCrear</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">usuario</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">UsuarioValido</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">SesionDB</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">nuevo</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Pedido</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">usuario</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="s">"id"</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="o">**</span><span class="n">datos</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">model_dump</span><span class="p">())</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">add</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">nuevo</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">commit</span><span class="p">()</span>
    <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">refresh</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">nuevo</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">nuevo</span>


<span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span>
    <span class="s">"/usuarios/{usuario_id}/pedidos"</span><span class="p">,</span>
    <span class="n">response_model</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="nb">list</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">schemas</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">PedidoRespuesta</span><span class="p">],</span>
<span class="p">)</span>
<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">listar_pedidos_de_usuario</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">usuario</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">UsuarioValido</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">SesionDB</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">consulta</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">select</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Pedido</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="n">where</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">models</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">Pedido</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span> <span class="o">==</span> <span class="n">usuario</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="s">"id"</span><span class="p">])</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">db</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">scalars</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">consulta</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="nb">all</span><span class="p">()</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>La dependencia recibe <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">usuario_id</code> de la ruta, hace la llamada y devuelve los datos del usuario (un <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">dict</code> con el JSON que respondió el otro servicio).</p>

<p>Si algo falla, lanza una <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">HTTPException</code> y el endpoint <strong>no se ejecuta</strong>. Además, al ser una dependencia, puedes reutilizarla en cualquier ruta que necesite validar al usuario.</p>

<h4 id="dos-consejos-importantes">Dos consejos importantes</h4>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Pon siempre un timeout explícito.</strong> Sin él, si el otro servicio se cuelga, tu servicio también se queda esperando indefinidamente y el “cuelgue” se expandirá de un microservicio a otro.</li>
  <li><strong>El orden de los <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">except</code> importa</strong>: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">TimeoutException</code> es un caso particular de <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">RequestError</code>, así que debe ir <strong>antes</strong>.</li>
</ol>

<blockquote>
  <p><strong>Posible mejora avanzada</strong>: crear un <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">AsyncClient</code> en cada petición es sencillo pero poco eficiente, porque no reutiliza las conexiones. En un servicio real se crea un único cliente al arrancar la aplicación y se comparte, pero nosotros no lo haremos para simplificar.</p>
</blockquote>

<h4 id="pruébalo">¡Pruébalo!</h4>

<p>Con los dos servicios en marcha, puedes realizar estas comprobaciones en Postman y, si todo ha salido bien, deberían funcionar:</p>

<ol>
  <li>Crea un usuario en <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">POST :8001/usuarios</code>.</li>
  <li>Crea un pedido con <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">POST :8002/usuarios/1/pedidos</code> y el cuerpo <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">{"descripcion": "Teclado mecánico", "importe": 59.9}</code>. Debe devolver <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">201</code> (éxito), porque el usuario <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">1</code> existe (lo acabas de crear).</li>
  <li>Prueba con un usuario inexistente (como <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">/usuarios/999/pedidos</code>): debes obtener un <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">404</code> (not found).</li>
  <li>Desactiva al usuario con <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">PATCH :8001/usuarios/1/desactivar</code> y repite el pedido. Ahora debes obtener un <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">403</code> (forbidden).</li>
  <li><strong>Apaga el servicio de usuarios</strong> (Ctrl+C) y repite el pedido. El error debe ser ahora un <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">503</code>. El servicio de pedidos sigue vivo y responde con un error controlado en lugar de petar.</li>
</ol>

<h4 id="consultar-varios-servicios-a-la-vez">Consultar varios servicios a la vez</h4>

<p>Si el microservicio de pedidos necesitase comprobar más cosas de otros microservicios, no solo el usuario, podrías usar <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">asyncio.gather</code> para lanzar <strong>las dos consultas a la vez</strong>. Por ejemplo:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="nn">asyncio</span>

<span class="k">async</span> <span class="k">with</span> <span class="n">httpx</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">AsyncClient</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">timeout</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mf">3.0</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="k">as</span> <span class="n">cliente</span><span class="p">:</span>
    <span class="n">resp_usuario</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">resp_producto</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="k">await</span> <span class="n">asyncio</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">gather</span><span class="p">(</span>
        <span class="n">cliente</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sa">f</span><span class="s">"</span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">USUARIOS_URL</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s">/usuarios/</span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">usuario_id</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s">"</span><span class="p">),</span>
        <span class="n">cliente</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">get</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sa">f</span><span class="s">"</span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">CATALOGO_URL</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s">/productos/</span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">producto_id</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s">"</span><span class="p">),</span>
    <span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Si cada consulta tarda 200 ms, en conjunto tardan unos 200 ms y no 400, que es lo que tardaría si hicieras primero una y luego otra.</p>

<h3 id="654-middlewares">6.5.4. Middlewares</h3>

<p>Un <strong>middleware</strong> es código que se ejecuta <strong>en cada petición</strong> antes de que el endpoint tome el control y/o después de que el endpoint responda.</p>

<p>Es, por tanto, el mismo concepto que los <em>middlewares</em> de Laravel. Sirven para tareas como registrar logs, medir tiempos, añadir cabeceras, comprobar autenticación…</p>

<p>Un middleware en FastAPI es una función <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">async def</code> decorada con <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">@app.middleware("http")</code>. Este, por ejemplo, mide cuánto tarda cada petición:</p>

<div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="nn">time</span>

<span class="kn">from</span> <span class="nn">fastapi</span> <span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">Request</span>

<span class="o">@</span><span class="n">app</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">middleware</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"http"</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="k">async</span> <span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">medir_tiempo</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">request</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">Request</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">call_next</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="n">inicio</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">time</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">perf_counter</span><span class="p">()</span>
    <span class="n">respuesta</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="k">await</span> <span class="n">call_next</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">request</span><span class="p">)</span>         <span class="c1"># aquí se ejecuta el endpoint
</span>    <span class="n">duracion_ms</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="n">time</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">perf_counter</span><span class="p">()</span> <span class="o">-</span> <span class="n">inicio</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="o">*</span> <span class="mi">1000</span>
    <span class="n">respuesta</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">headers</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="s">"X-Process-Time-ms"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="sa">f</span><span class="s">"</span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">duracion_ms</span><span class="si">:</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="n">f</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s">"</span>
    <span class="k">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sa">f</span><span class="s">"</span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">request</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">method</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s"> </span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">request</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">url</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">path</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s"> -&gt; </span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">respuesta</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">status_code</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s"> (</span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">duracion_ms</span><span class="si">:</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="n">f</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s"> ms)"</span><span class="p">)</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">respuesta</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Lo que hay antes de la línea <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">await call_next(request)</code> se ejecuta <strong>en el camino de ida</strong> (antes de ejecutar el endpoint); lo que hay después, <strong>en el camino de vuelta</strong> (al terminar el endpoint, antes de enviar la respuesta).</p>

<p>En la práctica final vas a tener que preparar un pequeño middleware para hacer un log de depuración.</p>
